.\" ABSD manual page source (mdoc(7)); rendered by scripts/render-man.sh.
.Dd September 27, 2026
.Dt REBOOT 8
.Os ABSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm reboot
.Nd restart a served ABSD machine
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is
.Ql shutdown -r now :
the SSH server ends every session in order, the file server commits and
stops, and init restarts the machine, which boots the same image again.
It takes no arguments.
Ask with
.Ql ssh host reboot
or type it to an interactive
.Xr absd-sh 1 ;
see
.Xr shutdown 8
for what happens, who may ask, and the exit status.
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
On the serial console the sequence of
.Xr shutdown 8
with
.Ql action=restart ,
then
.Ql MACHINE RESTART ARMED pid=1
and
.Ql MACHINE RESTART .
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr absd-sh 1 ,
.Xr shutdown 8
.Sh QUALIFICATION
Qualified under QEMU's i440fx machine, which resets on the first of the
three methods the kernel tries (the 0xcf9 reset register, the keyboard
controller, a triple fault).
QEMU must be allowed to reboot: under
.Fl no-reboot
without
.Fl no-shutdown
it exits with status 0 instead, and with both it pauses.
None of the three methods is tested on a physical machine.
